<h3>About General Physics I for Calculus Majors</h3>
<p>General Physics I for Calculus Majors is the first of two books of a calculus -based -physics course. It provides a rigorous introduction to the fundamentals of Newtonian mechanics. Further topics include oscillatory motion, resonance, mechanical waves, sound, standing waves, and superposition, and Newton's law of universal gravitation and orbital motion. The course builds upon OpenStax College Physics.</p>
